        <definition>static constexpr SPIFrame tle92466ed::SPIFrame::MakeRead</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint16_t addr) noexcept</argsstring>
        <name>MakeRead</name>
        <qualifiedname>tle92466ed::SPIFrame::MakeRead</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>uint16_t</type>
          <declname>addr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Construct read frame (without CRC - must be calculated separately) </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>addr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Register address (10-bit actual address, 0x000-0x3FF) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><ref refid="uniontle92466ed_1_1SPIFrame" kindref="compound">SPIFrame</ref> configured for read operation (CRC = 0)</para>
</simplesect>
Read frame format per datasheet: <verbatim>*  Bits 31-24 | Bits 23-17 | Bit 16 | Bits 15-0
* ------------+------------+--------+-----------
*  CRC (8-bit)| Don&apos;t Care |  R/W   | Address (7-bit)
*             |            |  0=R   |
* </verbatim></para>
<para>Note: read frames carry the FULL 16-bit address in bits [15:0]; bits [23:17] are don&apos;t-care (datasheet §5.2.3.2). This is deliberately different from the write frame, which has only a 7-bit address field. That asymmetry is why read-only status registers at 0x0200+ are reachable at all — they cannot be expressed in a write frame. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="inc/tle92466ed_spi_interface.hpp" line="266" column="30" bodyfile="inc/tle92466ed_spi_interface.hpp" bodystart="266" bodyend="273"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="uniontle92466ed_1_1SPIFrame_1aec6903aac37ef52ecfea43c68d372e6d" prot="public" static="yes" constexpr="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" noexcept="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>constexpr <ref refid="uniontle92466ed_1_1SPIFrame" kindref="compound">SPIFrame</ref></type>
        <definition>static constexpr SPIFrame tle92466ed::SPIFrame::MakeWrite</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint16_t addr, uint16_t data) noexcept</argsstring>
        <name>MakeWrite</name>
        <qualifiedname>tle92466ed::SPIFrame::MakeWrite</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>uint16_t</type>
          <declname>addr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint16_t</type>
          <declname>data</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Construct write frame (without CRC - must be calculated separately) </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>addr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Register address (10-bit actual address, 0x000-0x3FF) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Data word to write (16-bit) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><ref refid="uniontle92466ed_1_1SPIFrame" kindref="compound">SPIFrame</ref> configured for write operation (CRC = 0)</para>
</simplesect>
Write frame format per datasheet: <verbatim>*  Bits 31-24 | Bits 23-17 | Bit 16 | Bits 15-0
* ------------+------------+--------+-----------
*  CRC (8-bit)| Address(7) |  R/W   | Data (16)
*             |            |  1=W   |
* </verbatim></para>
<para>Note: the write address field is only 7 bits wide (datasheet §5.2.3.1), so <computeroutput>addr &amp; 0x7F</computeroutput> is not a truncation — every writable register on this device lives at 0x000..0x07F (central config 0x00..0x3F, channel config CH4 0x20.. through CH3 0x70..0x7E). Registers at 0x0200+ are read-only by construction: they cannot be addressed by a write frame at all. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="inc/tle92466ed_spi_interface.hpp" line="296" column="30" bodyfile="inc/tle92466ed_spi_interface.hpp" bodystart="296" bodyend="303"/>
      </memberdef>
