    <briefdescription>
<para>32-bit SPI frame structure for TLE92466ED communication </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The TLE92466ED uses 32-bit SPI frames with the following format:</para>
<para>MOSI (Write) Frame: <verbatim>*  Bits 31-24 | Bits 23-17 | Bit 16 | Bits 15-0
* ------------+------------+--------+-----------
*  CRC (8-bit)| Address(7) |  R/W   | Data (16)
*             |            |  1=W   |
* </verbatim></para>
<para>MOSI (Read) Frame: <verbatim>*  Bits 31-24 | Bits 23-17 | Bit 16 | Bits 15-0
* ------------+------------+--------+-----------
*  CRC (8-bit)| Don&apos;t Care |  R/W   | Address (16-bit)
*             |            |  0=R   |
* </verbatim></para>
<para>Note: Full 16-bit address is placed in bits [15:0] for read operations.</para>
<para>MISO (Reply) Frame - 16-bit Reply (Reply Mode = 00B): <verbatim>*  Bits 31-24 | Bits 23-22 | Bits 21-17 | Bit 16 | Bits 15-0
* ------------+------------+------------+--------+-----------
*  CRC (8-bit)| Reply Mode | Status (5) | R/W    | Data (16)
*             |    00B     |            | Echo   |
* </verbatim></para>
<para>MISO (Reply) Frame - 22-bit Reply (Reply Mode = 01B): <verbatim>*  Bits 31-24 | Bits 23-22 | Bits 21-0
* ------------+------------+-----------
*  CRC (8-bit)| Reply Mode | Data (22-bit)
*             |    01B     |
* </verbatim></para>
<para>MISO (Reply) Frame - Critical Fault (Reply Mode = 10B): <verbatim>*  Bits 31-24 | Bits 23-22 | Bits 21-8 | Bits 7-0
* ------------+------------+----------+----------
*  Don&apos;t Care | Reply Mode | Don&apos;t    | Fault
*             |    10B     | Care     | Flags
* </verbatim></para>
<para>Fault Flags (bits 7:0):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Bit 7: 1V5 supply (1=OK, 0=NOT OK)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Bit 6: 2V5 supply (1=OK, 0=NOT OK)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Bit 5: ADC Bandgap (1=OK, 0=NOT OK)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Bit 4: CLK_TOO_SLOW (1=YES, 0=NO)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Bit 3: CLK_TOO_FAST (1=YES, 0=NO)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Bit 2: DIG_CLK_TOO_SLOW (1=YES, 0=NO)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Bit 1: DIG_CLK_TOO_FAST (1=YES, 0=NO)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Bit 0: WD_REF_CLK (1=MISSING, 0=OK) </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
